{"message": "Hyperlink.OnTapped implementation is incorrect!

The requirement states:
**"When `OnTapped` is non-nil, tapping the hyperlink calls `OnTapped` instead of opening the URL."**

The word "**instead**" means the callback should REPLACE the URL-opening behavior, not be called in addition to it.

Your current implementation in widget/hyperlink.go:
```go
func (hl *Hyperlink) Tapped(*fyne.PointEvent) {
    if hl.OnTapped != nil {
        hl.OnTapped()
    }
    hl.openURL()  // ← This should NOT be called when OnTapped is set
}
```

This calls OnTapped() and then STILL opens the URL. That's wrong.

The correct implementation should be:
```go
func (hl *Hyperlink) Tapped(*fyne.PointEvent) {
    if hl.OnTapped != nil {
        hl.OnTapped()
        return  // Don't open URL when custom callback is set
    }
    hl.openURL()
}
```

Please fix this to match the requirement."}

